cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Zyxilon Explorer // IGNIS code or processed harmonization datasets, please cite this work using the metadata below."
title: "Zyxilon Explorer // IGNIS: MODIS-VIIRS Harmonization, 80% LOYO Prediction Intervals & +24h/+48h/+72h Wildfire Forecasting"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-19"
url: "https://zyxilon.proyectxor.site/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CE-GR/zyxilon-explorer"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"
authors:
  - family-names: "Guillermo"
    given-names: "Carlos"
  - name: "Zyxilon Explorer // IGNIS Team"
abstract: >-
  Open-science Earth observation platform built for the 2026 NASA International Space Apps
  Challenge (Harmonization of MODIS and VIIRS Hot Spots). Combines 27 years (2000-2026)
  of harmonized fire-hotspot climatology over a 0.1-degree (465-cell) Dominican Republic grid
  (with Uber H3 Res. 8 episode clustering), asymmetric 80% LOYO prediction intervals for counts
  and Fire Radiative Power (MW), an independent hierarchical Empirical-Bayes shrinkage benchmark,
  a 100-month pre-EOL Suomi-NPP to NOAA-20 cross-check, and a live FastAPI cartographic cockpit
  with calibrated +24h/+48h/+72h DR daily (ROC-AUC 0.818) and global GFA (ROC-AUC 0.941) forecasts.
  Code is licensed under MIT; processed datasets under data/processed/ are licensed under CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - MODIS
  - VIIRS
  - NASA FIRMS
  - wildfire harmonization
  - leave-one-year-out cross-validation
  - prediction intervals
  - Fire Radiative Power
  - Dominican Republic
  - NASA Space Apps Challenge
